    {
      "say": "When Things Fall Apart takes its title from Yeats, or Wide Sargasso Sea answers Jane Eyre, one text is talking to another. In the late 1960s the critic Julia Kristeva named this intertextuality: the idea that every text is a mosaic built from other texts. The web shows some famous conversations between books.",
