    {
      "say": "Sort the ways texts borrow. An allusion is a brief, deliberate nod, like a title or a name. Parody imitates in order to mock. Pastiche imitates playfully, without mockery. And rewriting retells a story from a new angle, as Wide Sargasso Sea does. Can you think of a film that does one of these?",
